  "Question": "The cost \\(C\\) of sending a parcel post package weighing \\(P\\) pounds, \\(P\\) an integer, is \\(10\\) cents for the first pound and \\(3\\) cents for each additional pound. The formula for the cost is:",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(C=10+3P\\)",
    "B": "\\(C=10P+3\\)",
    "C": "\\(C=10+3(P-1)\\)",
    "D": "\\(C=9+3P\\)",
    "E": "\\(C=10P-7\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "C",
  "Solution": "For a positive integer weight \\(P\\ge1\\), one pound is already covered by the \\(10\\)-cent first-pound charge. That leaves \\(P-1\\) additional pounds, each costing \\(3\\) cents.\n\nThus, with \\(C\\) measured in cents,\n\\[\nC=10+3(P-1),\n\\]\nchoice C.",
